# Example captain messaging gate (fork-only firstmate feature).
#
# Copy this file to config/captain-msg.env (gitignored, local) to OPT IN.
# Presence of that file is the whole gate: with it, firstmate wires the inbound
# poll and shares the ClickStack receiver's listener process on /captain-msg,
# and bin/fm-captain-msg.sh is willing to send. Without it, both are inert -
# the send tool refuses with a one-line message and the route answers 404.
#
# Unlike the ClickStack gate, the three keys below have NO safe default: a
# present-but-incomplete file is treated as a misconfiguration (loud failure),
# not "feature off". Every value here is non-secret (SIDs and a public URL) -
# the actual Twilio secrets live in 1Password, never in this file.
#
# See docs/captain-messaging.md for the full contract: authority, the speech
# contract every outbound message must pass, and setup.

# The captain's phone number in E.164 (e.g. +614xxxxxxxx). The only destination
# bin/fm-captain-msg.sh will ever send to, and the only sender inbound replies
# are accepted from.
CAPTAIN_MSG_DESTINATION=

# Twilio Account SID (starts with AC). Needed to address the Messages REST
# resource even when authenticating with a Restricted API Key.
CAPTAIN_MSG_ACCOUNT_SID=

# Twilio Messaging Service SID (starts with MG) whose sender pool holds the RCS
# Business sender ("Teslemetry") and nothing else - no phone number, so no
# automatic SMS fallback.
CAPTAIN_MSG_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=

# The exact public HTTPS URL Twilio POSTs inbound replies to (paste this same
# URL into the Twilio console's webhook configuration). Must match
# byte-for-byte: it is part of the signature Twilio computes.
# Default: https://fm.ba.id.au/captain-msg
#CAPTAIN_MSG_WEBHOOK_URL=https://fm.ba.id.au/captain-msg

# 1Password vault and item names holding the Twilio credentials. Defaults match
# this fork's existing "Twilio" item in vault "CLI":
#   CAPTAIN_MSG_OP_ITEM (username=Restricted API Key SID, credential=its
#     secret) - used for outbound sends.
#   CAPTAIN_MSG_OP_AUTHTOKEN_ITEM (credential=Twilio Account Auth Token) - a
#     SEPARATE item, because Twilio always signs inbound webhooks with the
#     Account Auth Token, never an API key secret.
#CAPTAIN_MSG_OP_VAULT=CLI
#CAPTAIN_MSG_OP_ITEM=Twilio
#CAPTAIN_MSG_OP_AUTHTOKEN_ITEM=Twilio Auth Token
